## 4. Content Standards

These are the lessons learnt across the documentation iterations. Apply all of them.

### 4.0 Application Overview Table (§1)

The §1 Application Overview is a single, full-width, two-column key/value table that acts as the at-a-glance project metadata sheet. Every Mule API document — regardless of layer (`exp` / `proc` / `sys`) — must use the same row schema, in the same order, so readers can scan across projects consistently.

#### 4.0.1 Column definition

| Column | Header | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | `Title` | The metadata field name. Render verbatim from the schema below. |
| 2 | `Description` | The resolved value for this project. Leave blank if truly unknown — never invent. |

> Note: column header is `Title` / `Description` (not `Field` / `Value`) to match the existing Confluence Sample documents under SampleConfluenceDocuments folder.

#### 4.0.2 Canonical row schema (preserve order)

| # | Title | What to populate it with | Source |
|---|-------|--------------------------|--------|
| 1 | Application Technical Name | The deployable artefactId, e.g., `drupal-exp-api`, `leads-proc-api`, `sfl-crm-persona-sys-api`. | `pom.xml` → `<artifactId>` |
| 2 | Application Business Name | Human-readable name, e.g., `Drupal Experience API`, `Lead Process API`, `SF Leads System API`. | `pom.xml` → `<name>` or project README |
| 3 | Business Domain | Domain area, e.g., `Persona Account`, `Person Domain`, `Order Management`. | Architecture/sprint docs |
| 4 | Available Versions | Semver list, e.g., `1.0`, `1.0, 1.1`. | `pom.xml` → `<version>` + Exchange |
| 5 | Purpose of API | One- or two-line summary of *what* the API does and *why*. | RAML root `description` / README |
| 6 | Mule Application Type | `API` for REST, `Batch`, `Scheduler`, `MQ Consumer`, etc. | Project type |
| 7 | API Type | `Experience` / `Process` / `System`. | Layer suffix in artefactId |
| 8 | GitHub Repo URL | Full HTTPS URL to the repo. | Git remote / CI config |
| 9 | Healthcheck Endpoints | Space- or bullet-separated list, e.g., `GET /health-check`, `GET /ping`. | RAML |
| 10 | Exchange Specification URL | Anypoint Exchange asset URL. | Exchange |
| 11 | Monitoring Dashboard URL | CloudHub/Anypoint Monitoring or Splunk/Datadog dashboard. | Ops runbook |
| 12 | API Manager URL | Anypoint API Manager instance URL. | Anypoint Platform |
| 13 | Runtime URLs | Public/CloudHub URLs per environment, one per line (`dev`, `qa`, `uat`, `prod`). | Deployment config |
| 14 | Postman Collection File | Path or Confluence attachment name of the Postman collection. | `/postman/` folder or attachment |
| 15 | Properties Configured | Comma- or line-separated list of files, e.g., `config.properties`, `config-dev.properties`, `config-qa.properties`, `config-uat.properties`, `config-prod.properties`. | `src/main/resources/properties/` |
| 16 | Azure Vault Keys and Credentials Details | Names of secret keys consumed (do **not** print values), e.g., `client.id`, `client.secret`, `salesforce.password`. | `secure-properties` + Azure Key Vault names |
| 17 | Depends on Mule Apps/APIs | Newline-separated list of downstream Mule apps/APIs invoked, e.g., `leads-proc-api`, `sfl-crm-sys-api`, `sfl-consents-sys-api`. | `global-config.xml` HTTP requests + RAML |
| 18 | Insulet Connectors/Libraries Used | Bullet list of internal Insulet libs, e.g., `Common Error Handler`, `Notification Connector`, `Common Logger`. | `pom.xml` `<dependencies>` |
| 19 | Other Libraries and Connectors Used | Third-party connectors, e.g., `HTTP Request Connector`, `Salesforce Connector`, `IBM MQ Connector`. | `pom.xml` `<dependencies>` |
| 20 | API Manager Policies Applied | Comma-separated list, e.g., `Client ID Enforcement`, `JWT Validation`, `Rate Limiting`. | API Manager / `auto-discovery` |
| 21 | Parent-POM | Parent POM coordinates, e.g., `mule-common-pom:1.x.x`. | `pom.xml` → `<parent>` |

